<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-kl2z6 increment 2 / nexus-vc6dh — plain btree index on
    staging.document_chunks(chash).

    Design of record: T2 nexus/design-kl2z6-combined-write [21804] REV 2
    §4.2 (the third sweep guard — "the sweep may delete a chunk only when
    no live declaration of intent references it"). The guard's two NOT
    EXISTS clauses (CatalogRepository.stagingGuardCondition) keep the
    function on the BOUNDED OUTER side (the per-doc dropped-chash
    candidate set, capped by the flush chunk cap) and probe
    staging.document_chunks BY chash — a probe the table's PK
    (tenant_id, doc_id, position) cannot serve at all (chash is not a
    prefix of that key). Without this index the guard's two NOT EXISTS
    subqueries force a full Seq Scan of staging.document_chunks per
    candidate row; nexus-vc6dh's 300K-row repro measured a REV-1 shape
    (function on the staging side, no usable index) at ~1s per sweep under
    the sweep's own EXCLUSIVE gate. WITH this index, the REV-2 corrected
    guard shape (function on the bounded outer side) plans as a genuine
    Index Scan on this index, ~600x faster on the same fixture (nexus-vc6dh).

    Zero cost outside an active guided migration: staging.document_chunks
    is empty in steady state (staging-001-landing-tables.xml's own
    javadoc — TRUNCATE-after-verify via /v1/staging/clear), so this index
    stays tiny and the sweep's own conditional-skip
    (CatalogRepository.stagingHasRowsForTenant) means the guard predicates
    referencing it are not even added to the DELETE unless staging holds
    rows for the sweeping tenant.

    PRECONDITION DISCIPLINE (catalog-013 / vectors-003 lineage): whole-
    changeset <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"> gated on a sqlCheck
    counting only VALID indexes of the target name — a manually pre-built
    valid index marks ran; an INVALID leftover does not satisfy the check,
    so CREATE INDEX runs, collides with the leftover's name, and halts the
    migration loudly (no silent masking). onError stays HALT (unset).

    BUILD-WINDOW: plain CREATE INDEX, not CONCURRENTLY — staging tables are
    a one-shot landing area (never serving-path) and, per the zero-cost
    note above, are empty at every fresh boot; even a populated store's
    staging table is bounded by one migration wave's chunk count, not the
    corpus at large. Liquibase runs in the boot-time migration window
    before the engine serves traffic; a narrow single-column btree over
    that row count builds well within the window.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="staging-2-document-chunks-chash-index" author="nexus-kl2z6.2">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pg_index i JOIN pg_class c ON c.oid = i.indexrelid JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = c.relnamespace WHERE n.nspname = 'staging' AND c.relname = 'idx_staging_document_chunks_chash' AND i.indisvalid</sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>staging.document_chunks(chash) — the nexus-kl2z6/vc6dh sweep staging-guard probe index; the table's PK leads with (tenant_id, doc_id, position) and cannot serve a chash-only lookup</comment>
        <sql>
CREATE INDEX idx_staging_document_chunks_chash
    ON staging.document_chunks (chash);
        </sql>
        <rollback>DROP INDEX IF EXISTS staging.idx_staging_document_chunks_chash</rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
